# Working directories, not part of the starter attendees clone: the raw kit
# drop, and the notes and specs written while building the guide.
miris-web-kit/
docs/

# The room and the props are IN the repo now. The workshop could not be run
# from a clean clone without them: nothing here was tracked, so step 01.1 drew
# an empty room and 03.1 dressed it with nothing.
#
# room.glb is the slimmed one -- 15.4MB to 1.6MB. Textures to webp, then weld
# and quantize. NOT `gltf-transform optimize`: its join/dedup pass merges
# meshes, 100 of them down to 43, and 02.1 matches materials BY MESH NAME, so
# the whole materials step silently stops working. Structure-preserving passes
# only.
public/env/*
!public/env/room.glb
!public/env/white-chapel.hdr

# CGAxis assets (public/tex/vault, public/props/vault) are tracked here by an
# explicit decision: this is a controlled demo and the build is not
# redistributed. Their licence still forbids redistribution in any form or at
# any resolution, so that decision is load-bearing, not a licence change --
# THE PUBLIC MIRROR MUST NOT RECEIVE THEM. AGENTS.md's publish filter strips
# both directories; do not remove those --path arguments.
# See public/tex/vault/SOURCES.md for what they are and how to re-fetch them.
